    "_comment_AWS_AIDLC_DEFAULT_SCOPE": "Pre-set default scope for /aidlc workflows. Valid: enterprise, feature, mvp, poc, bugfix, refactor, infra, security-patch, classic, workshop, express. Applies at workflow init only. See docs/guide/13-customization.md § Per-Project Default Scope.",
    "AWS_AIDLC_DEFAULT_SCOPE": "classic",
    "_comment_AIDLC_DISABLE_USAGE_TRACKING": "Set to \"1\" to turn off local token/cost tracking and remove the statusline cost segment. The statusline $ is a list-price estimate, not a bill; set this if you'd rather not show it, e.g. while presenting or screen-sharing. To price it at your own rates instead, set AIDLC_MODEL_RATES to a rates file. See docs/guide/15-troubleshooting.md § Statusline shows a cost segment you don't want."
